;; The package arbace/repr/go/gccompile (doc/go/GOI-SPEC.md, "Since v1: gc in the executable";
;; doc/go/GOI-DESIGN-REVIEW.md, Proposed 1 (b), the user's decision of 2026-11-22): gc's compiler,
;; cmd/compile of TamaGo's go1.27.1, run in the program, for goi's errorcheck of the programs whose
;; flags or errors need gc's own passes (arbace.repr.go.gc). Its main is cmd/compile's main.go,
;; ported as forms from tamago/cmd's (doc/ARBACE.md); gc itself is the renamed copy of tamago/cmd's
;; forms, arbace/repr/go/internal/gc/ (cmd's internal packages and the standard library's internal
;; ones are not importable from the program; bin/generated-check keeps the copy tamago/cmd's and
;; tamago/goroot's). Hand-written Go forms, printed with the program and listed in goi's table
;; (go/arbace/gotable.edn), so that Arbace calls Compile compiled.
(ns go.arbace.repr.go.gccompile
  (:require [arbace.go :as go]))

(go/package gccompile
  :path "arbace/repr/go/gccompile"
  :files ["compile.go"])

(load "gccompile/compile")
